<article class="env-definition" id="062K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/062K">Definition <span data-tag="062K">17.24.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a ringed space. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{O}_ X$ be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module map. The <em>Koszul complex</em> $K_\bullet (\varphi )$ associated to $\varphi $ is the sheaf of commutative differential graded algebras defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the underlying graded algebra is the exterior algebra $K_\bullet (\varphi ) = \wedge (\mathcal{E})$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the differential $d : K_\bullet (\varphi ) \to K_\bullet (\varphi )$ is the unique derivation such that $d(e) = \varphi (e)$ for all local sections $e$ of $\mathcal{E} = K_1(\varphi )$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>